A||N||2||turbo86se||16" wheels with lowered suspension||||5||
Z||000000||turbo86se||01-19-2000||01:40 AM||||<BR>Hey everyone, I know this question has been asked several times, but I haven't seen it asked with a lowered Fiero. I'm looking into a few sets of custom rims, all that I like are 16". If I were to put on 16" wheels, what is the best size that will work with my 86SE, that is lowered with Suspension Techniques springs, combined with KONI's if it matters. These 14" wheels gotta go!!  Thanks, and any help is appreciated! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||01-19-2000||02:35 AM||||You ask for best size?  I got 2cents.  16x7 rims in front with 225/50 and 16x8 rims in back with 245/50.  A very important point when changing rim widths is to keep the tread center aligned with the steering axis.  For every inch wider at the rim the backspacing has to be 1/2 inch deeper.  This also keeps the weight centered over the bearing.  Of course I had to dial in some oversteer before those tires became the best.||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||01-19-2000||06:37 PM||||That sounds like the setup I wanted,however,someone waved a set of nice 16X7,FWD wheels under my nose for a really good price and I bought them.I've got 205/55 in front,and 225/50 in the rear.Very well balanced,ride great,and also prefer a little oversteer dialed in,or more horsepower than I have now.||||reg||1
